    {
      "ESSeqNum": 0,
      "FacilityID": 1000124061,
      "SummaryText": "The Pittsburgh Paints Company (PPC) Huron, OH location is a 177800 square foot facility, that specializes in shipping, handling and storage of paints and commonly used consumable painting supplies. This facility currently handles and stores Aerosol paint, which constituents are the substances of consideration regarding RMP applicability. The site currently follows Applicable State, US EPA, Department of Transportation, NFPA, and OSHA requirements for the storage, handling and shipping of regulated items. Pittsburgh Paints Company also follows internal and local Emergency response policies and regularly works with regulating agencies and neighbors to foster a positive culture and community right to know. \nRegulated Substances/ Chemicals of Interest/ Process Chemicals\n\n   The PPC Huron Distribution Center stores paint in aerosol containers, of various sizes with a median average of one pound each container, for distribution to PPC owned stores, dealers and home centers throughout the United States.  These containers can contain one of the following: Propane, Methyl Ether, Isobutane and or Butane, which are used as propellants.  These materials are regulated as flammable substances under the EPA RMP regulations.\n\nThe site currently has various safe working systems in place. This includes \n\u0095\tNFPA compliant storage cages to contain incidents \n\u0095\tFacility wide sprinkler systems\n\u0095\tIn rack sprinkler systems within the designated storage cage\n\u0095\tElectric non sparking motorized equipment \n\u0095\tEmployee orientation and ongoing training\n\u0095\tMaterial handing work instructions\n\u0095\tIncident response measures\n\u0095\tSpill reporting procedures\n\n   To ensure a safe working environment and to mitigate the potential for a spill and or chemical release. PPC trains employees in the following:\n\u0095\tHazards of aerosols\n\u0095\tIncident reporting \n\u0095\tHAZARD Communications\n\u0095\tChemical spill reporting\n\u0095\tEmergency Response \n\u0095\tEmergency evacuation\n\u0095\tSafe Handling procedures\n\u0095\tMotorized Lift Operators Safety"
    }
  ]
